# Third party notices

Python runtime dependencies are pinned in `ml-service/requirements.lock`. Original dependency license files remain in installed distributions; system package copyright files remain under `/usr/share/doc` in the container.

| Component | Verified version | License / role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| pypdf | 6.10.0 | BSD-3-Clause; PDF inspection/native extraction |
| Beautiful Soup | 4.15.0 | MIT; primary news HTML extraction |
| Soup Sieve | 3.0.4 | MIT; HTML selectors |
| Tesseract OCR | 5.5.0, Debian 5.5.0-1+b1 | Apache-2.0; local OCR |
| Tesseract rus/eng data | Debian 1:4.1.0-2 | Apache-2.0; language data |
| Poppler utilities | 25.03.0, Debian 25.03.0-5+deb13u4 | GPL-2.0-or-later and component notices; separate pdftoppm process |
| FastAPI / Pydantic | 0.162.0 / 2.14.1 | MIT; API/contracts, inherited from ML branch |
| HTTPX / Uvicorn | 0.28.1 / 0.54.0 | BSD-3-Clause; HTTP/client/server, inherited from ML branch |
| IANA tz database (Debian `tzdata`) | from the base image | public domain; 03:00 Europe/Moscow reset of the ruble budget (`zoneinfo` from the Python standard library) |

The Dockerfile installs distribution packages; exact OS package versions can change with the base image repository. `tool_versions` records the actual OCR/render versions in every corpus. Distribution source/copyright locations are recorded in those packages' copyright files (Poppler: https://poppler.freedesktop.org/; Tesseract: https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/). Distributing a built image requires retaining the packages' notices and satisfying their applicable license/source obligations.

The fixed materials source registry covers the following publishers. Its HTTPS host/path restrictions and bounded request policy are project controls; they are not publisher-issued quotas. Source availability and release acceptance are recorded separately in `docs/materials-acceptance.md`.

| Publisher / material | Attribution and reuse reference | Project scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bank of Russia (`cbr_press`), primary press releases | [About the website](https://www.cbr.ru/about/); retain the original publisher link and publication date | [Press RSS](https://www.cbr.ru/rss/RssPress) and linked permitted press articles |
| Federal Tax Service (`fns_news`), primary news text | [Copyright notice](https://www.nalog.gov.ru/rn77/copyright/); retain an interactive source link and the original material separately from AI analysis | [Selected HTML news section](https://www.nalog.gov.ru/rn77/news/activities_fts/); excludes Internet services and regional RSS paths |
| U.S. Energy Information Administration (`eia_today`), its own public analytical text | [Copyrights and Reuse](https://www.eia.gov/about/copyrights_reuse.php); acknowledge EIA, publication date and original URL; identify any AI translation as a translation | [Today in Energy current HTML](https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/recent.php) and linked article text; excludes RSS, archives, third-party images/data and logos |

EIA publications retain their stated geography and forecast/conditional language. They are external public analysis; they are not Alfa-Bank assessments or facts about a Russian company. Raw article bodies remain private corpus inputs. The public repository contains synthetic fixtures and source metadata, without full publisher articles.

The existing request-time research tools separately fetch the CBR key rate table (`https://www.cbr.ru/hd_base/KeyRate/`), official exchange rates (`https://www.cbr.ru/scripts/XML_daily.asp`) and press releases. Indicators retain their effective dates and are not additional publishers. These tools use the shared controlled transport and local cache. Alfa-Bank hackathon PDFs and client CSV belong to their providers; raw files and OCR text are not redistributed in Git. Gold/review files contain IDs, hashes and evaluation metadata only.

Synthetic fixtures are marked as synthetic and do not constitute bank research or customer records. Offline test responses are scripted, not real model outputs. Generative models are remote services accessed through the hackathon gateway; this repository does not ship their weights. Only the six models listed by the case may be configured. The ruble guard counts only this service's own LLM calls with configured or conservative placeholder prices; it does not see other participants' spend on the shared key, so it does not by itself establish compliance with the shared daily monetary limit.
